rl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg/960px-Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg/500px-Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg","caption":"Hornstrandir","author":"Evgeniy Metyolkin","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westfjords_Region,_Iceland_-_panoramio_(17).jpg","ok_print":true}],"intro":{"lead":"Iceland's wild far corner: Dynjandi's bridal-veil falls, Latrabjarg puffin cliffs, empty fjords","facts":{"visit_h":3.8}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-dynjandi","name":"Dynjandi","kind":"Waterfall","lat":65.7325,"lon":-23.1986,"dist_km":47.0,"rank_score":9.34,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Dynjandi is a waterfall located in Arnarfjörður in the Westfjords region of Iceland. It is the largest waterfall in the Westfjords and has a total height of 100 metres (330 ft). Below it are five other waterfalls: Háifoss, Úðafoss, Göngufoss, Hundafoss and Bæjarfoss.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG/640px-Cascada_Dynjandi%2C_Vestfir%C3%B0ir%2C_Islandia%2C_2014-08-14%2C_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG","author":"Diego Delso","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cascada_Dynjandi,_Vestfir%C3%B0ir,_Islandia,_2014-08-14,_DD_136-138_HDR.JPG","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynjandi"},{"id":"hl-latrabjarg","name":"Latrabjarg","kind":"Cliffs","lat":65.5,"lon":-24.5,"dist_km":110.1,"rank_score":8.81,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Látrabjarg is a promontory in the Westfjords of Iceland, and the westernmost point in Iceland. The cliffs are home to millions of birds, including puffins, northern gannets, guillemots and razorbills. It is vital for their survival as it hosts up to 40% of the world population for some species such as the razorbill.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Iceland2008-Latrabjarg.cliff.JPG/640px-Iceland2008-Latrabjarg.cliff.JPG","author":"Progresschrome","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iceland2008-Latrabjarg.cliff.JPG","w":3072,"h":2048,"ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A1trabjarg"},{"id":"hl-isafjordur","name":"Isafjordur","kind":"Village","lat":66.0748,"lon":-23.1355,"dist_km":57.7,"rank_score":8.59,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"The lively capital of the Westfjords set on a dramatic fjord spit","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/%C3%8Dsafj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_12_June_2019.jpg/640px-%C3%8Dsafj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_12_June_2019.jpg","author":"Sturlast~iswiki","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%8Dsafj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_12_June_2019.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%8Dsafj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur"},{"id":"hl-drangajokull","name":"Drangajokull","kind":"Viewpoint","lat":66.183,"lon":-22.283,"dist_km":49.8,"rank_score":8.14,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Drangajökull is the northernmost glacier of Iceland, occupying the southern foothills of the Hornstrandir peninsula in the Westfjords region. It covers approximately 150 km2 and is the only Icelandic ice cap situated entirely below 1,000 metres in elevation. Lake sediment cores show that Drangajökull persisted near or above its present extent well into the mid-Holocene before retreating to near-modern limits between about 9,500 and 7,200 years ago.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Drangaj%C3%B6kull.jpg/640px-Drangaj%C3%B6kull.jpg","author":"AgainErick","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drangaj%C3%B6kull.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drangaj%C3%B6kull"},{"id":"hl-bolungarvik","name":"Bolungarvik","kind":"Village","lat":66.1517,"lon":-23.2561,"dist_km":67.4,"rank_score":7.61,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Bolungarvík is a small town and the only built-up area in the municipality of Bolungarvíkurkaupstaður in the northwest of Iceland, located on the Westfjords peninsula, approximately 14 km (8.7 mi) from the town of Ísafjörður and 473 km (294 mi) from the capital city Reykjavík.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Bolungarv%C3%ADk_2025_0974.jpg/640px-Bolungarv%C3%ADk_2025_0974.jpg","author":"Steinninn","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bolungarv%C3%ADk_2025_0974.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolungarv%C3%ADk"},{"id":"hl-vigur","name":"Vigur","kind":"Nature reserve","lat":66.0333,"lon":-22.8333,"dist_km":44.6,"rank_score":7.52,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Vigur is the second largest island of the Ísafjarðardjúp fjord in Westfjords, Iceland. Located just south of the Arctic Circle, the island is around 2 kilometres (6,600 ft) in length and 400 metres (1,300 ft) in width. The island is most noted for its thriving seabird colonies, traditional eiderdown production, and historical buildings.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Vigur.JPG/640px-Vigur.JPG","author":"Bromr","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vigur.JPG","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vigur"},{"id":"hl-hornstrandir","name":"Hornstrandir","kind":"Nature reserve","lat":66.4167,"lon":-22.5,"dist_km":77.0,"rank_score":7.33,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Hornstrandir is Iceland's northernmost peninsula, covering 580 km2 (220 sq mi) at the northern end of the Westfjords, to the north of the Jökulfirðir and to the northwest of Drangajökull glacier.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg/640px-Westfjords_Region%2C_Iceland_-_panoramio_%2817%29.jpg","author":"Evgeniy Metyolkin","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westfjords_Region,_Iceland_-_panoramio_(17).jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hornstrandir"},{"id":"hl-sudureyri","name":"Sudureyri","kind":"Village","lat":66.1281,"lon":-23.5333,"dist_km":75.5,"rank_score":6.41,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Suðureyri is a small Icelandic fishing village perched on the tip of the 13 km-long Súgandafjörður in the Westfjords.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Su%C3%B0ureyri_2025_0961.jpg/640px-Su%C3%B0ureyri_2025_0961.jpg","author":"Steinninn","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Su%C3%B0ureyri_2025_0961.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Su%C3%B0ureyri"},{"id":"hl-patreksfjordur","name":"Patreksfjordur","kind":"Village","lat":65.5936,"lon":-23.9958,"dist_km":85.1,"rank_score":6.41,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Patreksfjörður is a fishing village in the Westfjords of Iceland. It was an important fishing and trading post until the Icelandic government's introduction of a fishing quota in 1990. Administratively, it is part of the municipality of Vesturbyggð.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Patreksfj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_25.07.2025.png/640px-Patreksfj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_25.07.2025.png","author":"Vidirholm","licence":"CC BY 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patreksfj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur_25.07.2025.png","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patreksfj%C3%B6r%C3%B0ur"},{"id":"hl-raudisandur","name":"Raudisandur","kind":"Beach","lat":65.4661,"lon":-24.03,"dist_km":90.6,"rank_score":5.69,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"Rauðisandur is a coastal area in Westfjords, Iceland. Historically it was located in the historic Vestur-Barðastrandarsýsla county.","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/S%C3%B6%C3%B0udl1.jpg/640px-S%C3%B6%C3%B0udl1.jpg","author":"Xypete","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:S%C3%B6%C3%B0udl1.jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rau%C3%B0isandur"},{"id":"hl-vadalfjoll","name":"Vaðalfjöll","kind":"Peak","lat":65.58035,"lon":-22.0744,"dist_km":18.0,"rank_score":5.69,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Island%20Westfjorde%20161.JPG?width=960","author":"Zairon","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_Westfjorde_161.JPG","w":3444,"h":2586,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-galdrasyning-a-strondum","name":"Galdrasýning á Ströndum","kind":"Museum","lat":65.7066,"lon":-21.6656,"dist_km":23.3,"rank_score":5.69,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Holmav%C3%ADk%202.JPG?width=960","author":"Christian Bickel fingalo","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0 de","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/de/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Holmav%C3%ADk_2.JPG","w":3